 "PART_0D_PART_I_VERDICT": "No parameter-free feature separates strongly. Best is support count (cnt, AUC=0.611, 1.79x top-decile enrichment); F2 has the best enrichment (2.17x) despite a lower AUC (0.597). Direct query relevance (dense/splade/RRF) sits at pure chance (AUC 0.498-0.508), confirming the motivating hypothesis that direct lexical/dense relevance carries no signal for 3rd-hop answers. has_struct and best_core_rank are mildly ANTI-correlated (AUC<0.5) with being a still-missing required node -- among the hop3 residual specifically, structural support has already been exhausted by definition, so its presence stops being informative. Per the pre-committed decision rule: stop further L1 ranking work on MetaQA's hop3 residual and hand this discrimination problem to learned L2.",
